id: ops-kw02
title: Make historical Windows proof evidence available in fresh clones
description: "After merging reviewed repair PR #150 with main, CI run 38116691747 fails on Linux and Windows because test/windows-proof-history.test.ts loads test/windows-consumers.proof.ts from b89fd6f36adf91c9bfc784c7ab643d9ce9cb7eae, a development commit outside branch ancestry. The canonical object cache masks this failure. A fresh single-branch clone of #150 reproduces it. Preserve strict historical source-only proof refusal while replacing unavailable development-history dependencies with portable, provenance-linked evidence. This follow-up does not change reviewed repair behavior."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T06:12:11.492Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T08:18:17.988Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
parent: ops-hiee
repro_steps: "Clone the feature branch into a fresh repository and run node --test test/windows-proof-history.test.ts; git show b89fd6f36adf91c9bfc784c7ab643d9ce9cb7eae:test/windows-consumers.proof.ts fails."
expected_result: "Native proof controls and the missing-history diagnostic test run in a fresh clone using durable reachable history or reviewed committed fixtures, without skipped controls or weakened assertions."
actual_result: "CI Linux suite: 597 tests, 594 passed, 1 failed, 2 optional skips. Both Windows jobs fail the same historical proof test before native consumer controls. Fresh clone selected test: 0 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T08:16:31.940Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed root cause in CI run 38117928292 and a fresh single-branch clone: 1 test, 0 passed, 1 failed while loading b89fd6f proof source. Both checkout jobs already use fetch-depth: 0. Main 3fca1f2 has the same test; passing run 38122425892 includes c69400b, which independently replaces historical controls with frozen function strings. The feature merge did not introduce a separate checkout or test difference. Vendoring the complete pre-diagnostic proof preserves the explicit missing-history refusal test. Frozen old launcher functions preserve current consumer assertions; the availability guard names reachable main squash commit 3fca1f2. Preparing the same focused change in a separate main PR."
  "2026-10-11T08:16:57.359Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only replaceFunction with a no-op while retaining the new tests yields 2 tests, 1 pass, 1 failure. Removing only the explicit missing-history assertion from the native proof yields 2 tests, 1 pass, 1 failure. Both changes were restored; node --test test/windows-proof-history.test.ts and pm test ops-kw02 --run --progress each pass 2/2 with zero failures or skips. Linked result tracking is disabled by existing configuration, so this comment records the receipt."
  "2026-10-11T08:18:17.988Z",codex-agent,"The separate fix/vendor-historical-proof-fixture branch starts at origin/main 3fca1f2 and contains only durable Windows proof fixtures, function controls, regression coverage and this existing tracker item. Reusing ops-kw02 from the feature branch avoids a duplicate issue. The same two function/diagnostic behavioral revert checks apply; focused regression passes 2/2. Main has the same deleted-branch dependency and needs this fix independently of PR #150."
